{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:inflation:reconciler","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:ce97ee80a2067c5bf06c253ecaf71ae1dad364496d5f2b7b05d587a23bbf1b1c","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.27},"questionHash":"sha256:cfe468fa9439bedeee3804a35583667745f13831322e2c91a89c02a1b211413b","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq5","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"WEIGHTING: Resolution Auditor heaviest, because he produced the effort's two decisive readings and both survived adversarial review; Fermi heaviest on the multiplication; Inside-View credited for the shock-by-source taxonomy; Red-Team adopted on one point, rejected on another; Outside-View down-weighted (his conditional of 0.33 was derived from the naive \"stocks crashed AND yields rose\" scan that the Auditor showed is the wrong test).\n\nAUDITOR'S FIRST READING, ADOPTED BY EVERYONE AFTER HIM: the OR clause is VACUOUS. \"Rises >= 25 bps\" is a strict subset of \"fails to fall by >= 50 bps,\" so the operative test is only that G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominals do not rally 50 bp during the drawdown window — anything from -49 bp upward qualifies. This is far looser than the scan most forecasters run and it admits every muted-rally episode, not just 1973-74 and 2022.\n\nAUDITOR'S SECOND READING, ALSO ADOPTED: MOVE is yield-curve-weighted, basis-point-NORMALIZED 1-month implied vol, not log/relative, so its level scales with the yield level. It averaged ~60 in 2017-19 at ~2% yields, 120-130 in 2022-23, ~100-110 in 2024, and a 2025 close reported at 63.96. At 4-4.5% nominals the vol-neutral level is ~95-105, so a 105 hurdle is closer to \"rates stay here and nothing calms down\" than to \"a decade of crisis.\"\n\nCONJUNCT A (MOVE 10-yr average >= 105, 2027-2036) = 0.42. Fermi's two-phase build: 2027-2031 ~105 (fiscal/AI-capex/inflation-impulse phase, duration supply against dealer balance sheets, repression-versus-spiral belief dispersion), 2032-2036 ~90, average 97.5, sd ~12 on the decade average -> 1 - Phi(0.625) = 0.27, lifted to 0.34 for the bp-normalization tailwind at 4.5-5% nominals, less ~0.02 one-way for ICE methodology-change, re-basing or discontinuation risk over a ten-year window. I lift to 0.42 rather than the Red-Team's 0.55: his back half stays stressed at 95-115 purely because his drifted ~3% anchor persists, and I accept only part of that drift (see CQ2), but the Inside-View's assumption of a credible low-inflation equilibrium compressing back-half vol to 75-90 is too clean against a debt path that is still unresolved in 2036 and a CQ4 distribution that is genuinely bimodal.\n\nCONJUNCT B = 0.43. P(at least one >= 25% MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown in 10 years) = 0.83: base rate ~7-8 episodes in 55 years = ~0.135/yr gives 0.75, lifted for index concentration (~73% US, top-10 ~25% of float, heavily the AI complex), the ~$1.4T circular vendor/cloud/chip commitments on ~$300B equity and ~$650B debt, and the locked 66% AI-Q4. P(no 50 bp rally | drawdown) = 0.45: historically 2 clear failures of ~8 = 0.25, lifted because the test is the loose one above, because my CQ2 path has OECD core above target precisely in 2027-2030 when the capex-cycle shock is most likely, and because convenience-yield erosion plus levered basis-trade absorption make the 2020-style flight-to-quality less reliable — but NOT to the Red-Team's 0.55, which again rides his anchor. Expected qualifying attempts ~1.25 -> 1 - (0.55)^1.25 = 0.47, less 0.04 for the undefined \"during the equity drawdown window\" (on a loose within-window reading, long drawdowns such as 2000-02 almost always contain a 50 bp fall somewhere, flipping 1987 and 2000-02 to NO; I weight 70/30 toward endpoint-to-endpoint, per the Auditor). 0.43.\n\nCONJUNCTION: strongly positive — both conjuncts are readings of ONE institutional state (fiscal-dominance risk, leveraged duration absorption, unanchored term premium), not two independent draws. P(A|B) = 0.65 against an unconditional 0.42. JOINT = 0.43 x 0.65 = 0.280, less 0.02 for MOVE index-continuity and annul risk = 0.26 -> 27. PARTIAL, NOT FULL, CONJUNCTION DISCOUNT: the naive independent product is 0.18, and the near-co-determination is worth ~1.5x of it. I will not go to the Inside-View's or Red-Team's 34-38, which require conditionals of 0.50-0.55 on the yield leg.\n\nCOHERENCE CHECKS, STATED AS REQUIRED. (i) Against CQ4's variance: my interdecile span is 2.30 pp (1.05 to 3.35) around a 2.00 P50, i.e. high and bimodal-leaning rate uncertainty, which is what supports conjunct A at 0.42 against a ~0.27 unconditional base rate — a narrow CQ4 would have forced CQ5 toward 18. (ii) Against CQ6-C/D mass: C + D = 31. CQ5 at 27 is slightly below that and sits mostly inside it, which is right — the qualifying no-rally drawdown is overwhelmingly a C-type (inflation-correlated or sovereign-stress) event, with a minority in the D-type post-bust path where the shock is a growth-and-credit shock that normally BUYS a bond rally and therefore FAILS the test. CQ5 exceeds C alone (17) because the 2027-2030 buildout impulse supplies qualifying states on paths that nonetheless END in regime B, and the CQ5 window opens in 2027 while the CQ6 regimes are scored at Dec 2036.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:52.889Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"Turkish annual CPI, as published by TurkStat, averages below 7.0% over calendar 2027-2029 (arithmetic mean of the three December-on-December prints), with Mexico, Chile and Colombia each averaging below 3.5% over the same three years.\",\"by_when\":\"Jan 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The cleanest single falsifier of MY numbers, because I have made this term the largest and most mechanical in the payload. It removes the ~+0.30 pp EM-OECD floor: my GDP-weighted OECD-38 core central falls from ~2.65 to ~2.45 and P(core >= 2.50 over 2027-2036) drops from 0.58 to ~0.38, taking CQ2 from 38 to ~26. The 2032-2036 central falls from 2.35 to ~2.18, cutting CQ6-C from 17 to ~11 and raising CQ6-D from 14 to ~20, with B roughly unchanged at ~57. CQ4 P50 falls ~15 bp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"US CPI core commodities (core goods) 12-month rate at or below 0.0% for calendar-year 2029, while Section 301/232-style tariff coverage remains in force at or above 2026 breadth.\",\"by_when\":\"Jan 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the one Red-Team hit I partially adopted — downward nominal rigidity converting the relative-price skew into the level. My core-goods term reverts from 0.8% to the Wave-1 plug of ~0.4% (-0.09 pp on the US leg, ~-0.07 pp on the aggregate), and with it the whole claim that tariffs and fragmentation have changed the regime in sectors that 'want' to deflate. CQ2 falls from 38 to ~32; CQ6-C from 17 to ~13 with the mass to B; CQ5 conjunct A falls ~0.03, taking CQ5 from 27 to ~25. It would also mean the Red-Team contrarian-posed on his single largest departure from Wave 1 and I should not have moved at all.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"China headline CPI (NBS monthly series, any basket vintage) prints 2.0% year-on-year or higher for four consecutive quarters at any point between 2027 and 2031, with the non-food, non-residence component contributing at least 1.0 pp of it (i.e. not a pork or energy spike).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Kills CQ2's stronger conjunct and the China-as-semi-independent-deflationary-object premise my effort brief required me to carry. P(China CPI < 1.50% over 2027-2036) falls from 0.68 to ~0.38 and CQ2 drops from 38 to ~22 even with my OECD leg fully intact — which is the cleanest available test of whether my CQ2 comes from the OECD leg (my claim) or from the correlation assumption. It also lifts my China real leg from 3.05% toward 3.4%, raising CQ3 P50 from 1.75 to ~1.88 and shifting ~4 points of CQ6 mass out of D into B and C.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Cumulative publicly disclosed AI-related capex impairments and cancellations stay below 10% of announced hyperscaler buildouts AND net external AI software/API revenue exceeds 1.0x annualized AI compute D&A for four consecutive quarters, with at least 70 GW of net firm capacity serving data centres reaching commercial operation across OECD-38 + China (EIA / ENTSO-E / CEC commissioning data) by end-2031.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The highest-leverage signpost for my payload, because it removes the locked AI-Q4 bust from the middle of every 2032-2036 measurement window and simultaneously refutes my coupled claim that trades labour and interconnection bind harder than the dollars. Capital-services growth stays at ~1.8%/yr (+0.30 pp on the OECD leg) and the AI savings-demand term returns to +0.25 pp on r*. CQ3 P50 moves from 1.75 to ~2.05 and P90 from 2.75 to ~3.00; CQ4 P50 from 2.00 to ~2.30 with a thinner left tail; CQ6-A from 12 to ~19, D from 14 to ~9, B to ~57, C ~15; CQ5 falls from 27 to ~21 as the back-half MOVE path drops toward 85 and the leveraged-unwind shock source thins. It would also retire my AI-Q3 coupling correction.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"An equity drawdown of >= 20% (MSCI World, USD, closing basis) occurs in which the G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal sovereign yield FALLS by >= 100 bp between the equity peak date and the trough date — the classic flight-to-quality reasserting itself despite convenience-yield erosion, basis-trade absorption and >100% debt/GDP.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the fiscal-dominance correlation structure behind both CQ5 and CQ4's right tail. P(no 50 bp rally | drawdown) falls from 0.45 to ~0.28 and the A|B conditional from 0.65 to ~0.52, taking CQ5 from 27 to ~16. CQ4 P90 falls from 3.35 to ~2.95 and the distribution loses its right skew. ~3 points of CQ6 mass move from C to D, because bond-market tolerance means repression is unnecessary and accommodation of inflation is less likely.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'inflation'."}}